    "interpretation": [
      "Charged work and elapsed/CPU time are separate measurements.",
      "The 16-pattern, 10-prefix fixture at the production 4096 work cap completes 64 candidates instead of 59, with the same null improvement and five probes.",
      "The comparison of 4423 versus 2651 work for the same 64 candidates uses an external high-work diagnostic run; it does not change a production cap.",
      "Long-prefix fixtures improve, but the multi-fixture no-cache controls include small public-planner slowdowns. Retain all measurements; this is not a claim of universal speedup.",
      "One short-prefix helper varied substantially between measurement protocols. Profile/order sensitivity is a possible explanation, not a traced JVM cause; retain the isolated longer-warmup results alongside the multi-fixture results.",
      "The isolated short-prefix helper median CPU time decreases about 3.1%, but its P95 increases about 12.9%; there is no guarantee of deadline neutrality.",
      "Synthetic small DAG timings do not establish an improvement for large modpack graphs, which remain outside the 16-pattern admission gate."
    ]
